# Movie Tracker Initialization

Build a Movie Tracker application using Neon MCP database, Next.js 16, shadcn/ui, and Tailwind CSS.

## Features to Initialize

- Dashboard to view trending movies
- Search functionality to find movies by title
- Detail page for each movie showing its information
- Neon MCP database to store and retrieve movie data
- TMDB API to fetch movie details
- UI built with shadcn/ui components styled with Tailwind CSS

## Database Setup

1. Access the database and create a schema called `movies-tracker`
2. Reference the `database.mdc` rule for connection details and Neon MCP integration

## Steps

1. Set up Next.js 16 project with App Router
2. Configure Prisma ORM with Neon adapter
3. Set up TMDB API integration in `src/lib/tmdb.ts`
4. Create database schema with Prisma
5. Build trending movies dashboard page
6. Build movie search functionality
7. Build movie detail page
8. Configure shadcn/ui components
9. Apply Tailwind CSS styling
